  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to pass (an exam, test, audition)",
      "explanation": "To succeed in an examination or selection process. The intransitive counterpart of {受|う}ける, focusing on the result rather than the act of taking the test. The thing passed is marked with に."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "19367_ukaru_ex1",
      "japanese": "{試験|しけん}に{受|う}かった。",
      "english": "I passed the exam.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "19367_ukaru_ex2",
      "japanese": "{大学|だいがく}に{受|う}かるために{毎日|まいにち}{勉強|べんきょう}している。",
      "english": "I'm studying every day to get into university.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "19367_ukaru_ex3",
      "japanese": "{運転|うんてん}{免許|めんきょ}の{試験|しけん}に{一発|いっぱつ}で{受|う}かるのは{難|むずか}しい。",
      "english": "It's hard to pass the driver's license exam on the first try.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "notes": "{受|う}かる is an intransitive result verb — you do not actively \"do\" passing; rather, the result of passing happens to you. This contrasts with {受|う}ける, which describes the action of taking a test.\n\nUSAGE:\n- The exam or institution passed is marked with に: {試験|しけん}に{受|う}かる, {大学|だいがく}に{受|う}かる\n- The opposite is {落|お}ちる (to fail an exam)\n\nCONTRAST WITH {受|う}ける:\n- {受|う}ける means \"to take\" an exam (the action)\n- {受|う}かる means \"to pass\" an exam (the result)\n- {試験|しけん}を{受|う}ける = to take an exam\n- {試験|しけん}に{受|う}かる = to pass an exam\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {試験|しけん}に{受|う}かる — to pass an exam\n- {大学|だいがく}に{受|う}かる — to get into university\n- {面接|めんせつ}に{受|う}かる — to pass an interview\n- {一発|いっぱつ}で{受|う}かる — to pass on the first try",
